# Wave W17-V (Route 208): rest turf — rest-meadow turf: a warm easy green carrying soft warm flecks, the meadow where the file of travellers stretches out below the mountain’s south door (design: the domes shrink behind you; the mountain does not; foothill rest rocks line the bends). Route 208’s own ground — the warmest green in the tranche: split from Route 207’s glinting climb turf by the warmth and the missing glints (rest vs effort), and from Route 201’s fresh shore green by register (foothill ease vs first-road freshness).
